You are given a List<Product> containing duplicate product entries. Write Java code to remove the duplicates.

Assume the Product object contains fields such as:

productId
productName
price
lastUpdatedTime

Handle the following three cases:

Case 1: Keep the first occurrence
Two products are considered duplicates if they have the same productId.
Remove duplicate products and retain the first occurrence of each product.
Example:
Input:

101 - Laptop
102 - Mobile
101 - Laptop
103 - Tablet
102 - Mobile
Expected Output:
101 - Laptop
102 - Mobile
103 - Tablet
Ans:
import java.util.*;

public class ProductCleanup {

    public static List<Product> removeDuplicates(List<Product> products) {

        if (products == null || products.isEmpty()) {
            return Collections.emptyList();
        }

        Set<Long> seenProductIds = new HashSet<>();

        return products.stream()
                .filter(Objects::nonNull)
                .filter(product -> seenProductIds.add(product.getId()))
                .toList();
    }
}


Case 2: Keep the latest occurrence

If multiple products have the same productId, retain the latest product entry and remove the older duplicate entries.

Example:

Input:

101 - Laptop - 50000
102 - Mobile - 20000
101 - Laptop - 55000
103 - Tablet - 30000

Expected Output:

101 - Laptop - 55000
102 - Mobile - 20000
103 - Tablet - 30000

Explain how you would handle this using Java Collections or Streams.
Ans:
Map<Long, Product> uniqueProducts = products.stream()
        .filter(Objects::nonNull)
        .collect(Collectors.toMap(
                Product::getId,
                product -> product,
                (oldProduct, newProduct) -> newProduct,
                LinkedHashMap::new
        ));

Case 3: Remove duplicates based on the complete Product object

Consider two products duplicates only when all relevant fields of the Product object are equal.

Implement the solution using equals() and hashCode() and remove duplicate objects using Java Streams or Collections.
Ans:
List<Product> uniqueProducts = products.stream()
        .distinct()
        .toList();

